{"kind":"assert","text":"AR-4 read (cd9b8e19), from dap-grow archive-pass and archive-row diagnostics, 15:34Z-15:43Z (read-only):\n\n- Rules, Site and Room A (DOs 9ecbec54, 236dc9fd, e90a0152): one pass each at 15:35:15-27, step target, detail target-unbound, state disabled, reason unbound. Each stored its marker. No pass since.\n- Directory sc_cu5bjlh3 (DO 661c0b32): a pass every minute since 15:35:10 (15:36:12, 15:37:09 ... 15:43:10). Each ends target / target-unbound / disabled and stores the marker one day out.\n- Membership (DO e3b2c953): pin / disabled every minute, as before AR-4.\n\nCause of the extra ~6/min: the Directory object is constructed again each minute. Each pass is preceded by the constructor's one-time archive-row-diagnostic-v1 (object.ts:417-435), and it shows the previous marker still one day out and the platform alarm one day out. The constructor's production activation block (object.ts:374-379) then calls archive.committed(). My signal() treats any call on a Directory marker as a Directory commit and drops the marker, so every activation runs a full pass. The RPCs in the pass (nativeBirth, then archiveItem) are the Directory's own reads. I did not find what activates the Directory each minute.\n\nCost: about 6 DO requests a minute, about 360 an hour, worse than the 98 an hour before AR-4.\n\nFix (AR-5, one small head): activation calls committed() in a mode that leaves any unbound marker, and only a sealed commit (onSealed) drops the Directory's. Red: the installed fixture restarts the Directory after its marker and expects no pass. I can have the head ready in about 15 minutes, plus a gate. The other option is to deploy fc42cf3e to dap-grow until AR-5 lands. Which do you want?","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}